# Modern Docs-as-Code Strategy Blueprint

## Vision Statement
Migrate product documentation away from isolated silos into a centralized, developer-aligned **Docs-as-Code framework**. This strategy treats documentation exactly like software code—authored in Markdown, tracked in Git, peer-reviewed via Pull Requests, and deployed via automated CI/CD pipelines.

## Current vs. Target Architecture Analysis

| Operational Unit | Legacy Workflow | Target Docs-as-Code Environment |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Authoring Interface** | Confluence WYSIWYG Editor | Visual Studio Code / Markdown |
| **Version Tracking** | Page history snapshots | Git (Branches, Commits, Pull Requests) |
| **Review Execution** | Ad-hoc emails and chat threads | GitHub Pull Request Review Checklists |
| **Deployment Mechanism** | Manual page publishing | Automated CI/CD Execution Pipelines |

## Technology Stack Breakdown
*   **Source Language:** Extended Markdown (`CommonMark` compliant).
*   **Version Control Platform:** GitHub Enterprise.
*   **Static Site Generator (SSG):** Docusaurus / MkDocs Material.
*   **Validation Engines:** Markdownlint and Markdown-link-check.
